472222238779067993", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "168635192", "author": {"steamid": "76561198016711982", "personaname": "shirt", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198016711982/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 50, "playtime_forever": 101, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 101, "last_played": 1719778630, "avatar": "56f38b91a890f8456172fe7cb99d8f8dc72892a9"}, "language": "english", "review": "At anything above 90% discount, this game is NOT worth it.\n\nIn short, Back 4 Blood did everything wrong that Left 4 Dead did right. It's an uninspired heap of bad sound design, unsatisfying gunplay, redundant and unnecessary trading card systems, weird and cartoonish zombie design, and bad map design all built upon a physics engine that somehow feels more dated than Left 4 Dead's.\n\nThe UI is clunky. The movement is clunky. The AI is clunky. This whole game epitomizes CLUNK. Nothing feels smooth, the guns are not fun to shoot, the zombies are not fun to kill, the story is not fun. \n\nI genuinely struggled to play past the hour mark. I had to force myself to keep trudging through the story after the first couple of missions.\n\nFor 90% off, go for it. Not bad to kill an hour on. Anything more than $10 - don't bother.", "timestamp_created": 1719779139, "timestamp_updated": 1719779139, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.519890308380126953", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "reactions": []}]}